  "result": "Perfect! All 141 tests pass. Let me verify the implementation is complete:\n\n**Summary of Date Utilities Implementation:**\n\n1. **Created `src/dates.js`** with three utility functions:\n   - **`isValidDate(text)`**: Validates YYYY-MM-DD format and ensures the parsed date matches the input string (catches invalid dates like Feb 30, Feb 29 in non-leap years)\n   - **`addDays(date, n)`**: Adds n days to a date (can be negative), returns YYYY-MM-DD format\n   - **`daysBetween(a, b)`**: Calculates b minus a in whole days\n\n2. **Updated `createInvoice()`** to:\n   - Use `isValidDate()` instead of inline validation\n   - Simplified date validation from 4 lines to 1 line\n\n3. **All date operations use UTC**:\n   - `Date.prototype.getUTCFullYear()`\n   - `Date.prototype.getUTCMonth()`\n   - `Date.prototype.getUTCDate()`\n   - `Date.prototype.setUTCDate()`\n   - Never uses local timezone methods\n\n4. **Added 21 comprehensive tests** covering:\n   - Valid dates (including leap years)\n   - Invalid formats (wrong separator, wrong order)\n   - Invalid calendar dates (Feb 30, non-leap Feb 29, month 13, month 0)\n   - Edge cases (empty strings, null, undefined)\n   - Month and year boundaries\n   - Large date ranges\n   - Leap year vs non-leap year handling\n   - Inverse relationship verification (addDays + daysBetween are inverse operations)\n\nThe implementation correctly handles all edge cases and works entirely in UTC, avoiding local timezone issues.",
